From 8b7029c5dad40acd368ad1cb3ebe6b24a0563636 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AzediZ <145237384+AzediZ@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 00:34:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 103/110] Gas sites and signatures

The booster gas nebulae spawn as Ladar signatures in their Crucible
regions:  Mykoserocin mostly in the empire hot-spot constellations,
low-sec Cytoserocin in the empire regions' low sec, and null
Cytoserocin in the null hot-spot constellations, the bigger ones
guarded.  Dungeons can be bound to a region or constellation and carry
their own signature strength.  GM /gas lists the region's sites and
spawns one next to your ship (a random one in a system that gets
none).

Fixes rolled in:
- DED complexes spawn in known space, and wormhole systems get their
  ore sites and the right number of gas, data, relic and anomaly sites
  (MakeRandomInt never returned its upper bound)
- codebreakers, analyzers and salvagers open data and relic containers
  again, and the dungeon gets its hacking, archaeology and salvaging
  triggers, so those sites finish
